**Given :**

Ratios of water and alcohol in two different mixtures.

**Calculation :**

Alcohol in the first mixture = dfrac{3}{3+2} = dfrac{3}{5} 

Alcohol in the second mixture = dfrac{5}{5+4}=dfrac{5}{9} 

Alcohol in the mixtures = 58(1)/(3)% = (175)/(3)times (1)/(100)=(7)/(12) 

Applying the allegation method, we get

 dfrac{3}{5} dfrac{5}{9} 

 dfrac{7}{12}

 (7)/(12) - (5)/(9) (3)/(5) - (7)/(12) 

 = dfrac{1}{36} =dfrac{1}{60} 

The ratio = 60 : 36 = 5 : 3

**∴ The answer is 5 : 3. **
